# Tailwind v4 · Next.js · TypeScript — Cursor Rules

You are a senior frontend engineer on this project. The design system is fully
defined in `src/styles/globals.css`. Follow every rule below precisely. Never
justify deviating from them. When in doubt, check the token list in Section 1
before reaching for an arbitrary value.

---

## 1. PROJECT TOKENS — THE REAL TOKEN MAP

All tokens are defined in `src/styles/globals.css`. This is the canonical reference.
Never invent values — always use what exists here, or add a new token to the file.

### 1.1 Color tokens (use as Tailwind utilities)

Raw ramp lives in `:root` as `--g*` variables. Reference them only through
semantic `@theme` aliases below — never use `--g*` directly in component
`className` strings.

| Utility class | Token | Raw value |
|---|---|---|
| `text-text-default` | `--color-text-default` → `--g8` | `#121212` — primary text |
| `text-text-secondary` | `--color-text-secondary` → `--g6` | `#1c1c1c` |
| `text-text-subtle` | `--color-text-subtle` → `--g4` | `#86868a` — captions |
| `text-text-white` | `--color-text-white` → `--white` | `#ffffff` |
| `text-text-black` | `--color-text-black` → `--g8` | `#121212` |
| `bg-fill-default` | `--color-fill-default` | Page/panel surfaces (`html`, `body`, home shell, sky) |
| `bg-fill-dark` | `--color-fill-dark` → `--g8` | `#121212` — dark chrome (footer reveal) |
| `bg-fill-white` | `--color-fill-white` → `--white` | `#ffffff` |
| `border-line` | `--color-line` → `--g2` | `#d7d7d9` — dividers |
| `bg-hero-box` | `--color-hero-box` | `color-mix` from `--color-fill-default` at 50% |

Rules:
- `text-text-default` for primary body text (g8).
- `bg-fill-default` for page/section surfaces and `html` / `body` base (g3).
- `bg-fill-dark` for dark site chrome (footer reveal).
- `text-text-secondary` for slightly softer headings.
- `text-text-subtle` for captions, labels, metadata.
- `border-line` for ALL dividers and borders — never `border-gray-*`.
- Never use raw `--g*` variables in className. Never use hex colors in className.

### 1.2 Font family tokens

| Utility | Token | Maps to |
|---|---|---|
| `font-sans` | `--font-sans` | `var(--font-saans)` + system fallbacks |
| `font-serif` | `--font-serif` | `var(--font-crimson)` + system fallbacks |

- `--font-saans` and `--font-crimson` are injected by `next/font` as CSS variables.
  They must be declared on `<html>` in `src/app/layout.tsx`.
- Never use `font-['Inter']` or any hardcoded font name.

### 1.3 Spacing — named rhythm + Tailwind default scale

#### Named rhythm (semantic — prefer for section layout)
Use these for section-level padding and gaps that should tighten at ≤1280px.

| Utility | Token | Value (desktop) | Value (≤1280px) |
|---|---|---|---|
| `gap-xs` / `p-xs` | `--spacing-xs` | `8px` | `8px` |
| `gap-sm` / `p-sm` | `--spacing-sm` | `12px` | `12px` |
| `gap-md` / `p-md` | `--spacing-md` | `24px` | `20px` |
| `gap-lg` / `p-lg` | `--spacing-lg` | `48px` | `32px` |
| `gap-xl` / `p-xl` | `--spacing-xl` | `64px` | `64px` |

The `sm`, `md`, `lg` named spacers **respond automatically** via the
`@media (max-width: 1280px)` block in `:root`.

#### Tailwind v4 default scale (0.25rem steps — use for fixed UI details)
Base unit `0.25rem` (4px at 16px root). Examples:

| Utility | px |
|---|---|
| `p-0.5` / `gap-0.5` | 2px |
| `p-1` / `gap-1` | 4px |
| `p-2` / `gap-2` | 8px |
| `p-3` / `gap-3` | 12px |
| `p-4` / `gap-4` | 16px |
| `p-5` / `gap-5` | 20px |
| `p-6` / `gap-6` | 24px |
| `p-8` / `gap-8` | 32px |
| `p-12` / `gap-12` | 48px |
| `p-14` / `gap-14` | 56px |
| `p-16` / `gap-16` | 64px |

**Decision rule:**
- Major section padding/gaps → named rhythm (`px-lg`, `gap-md`).
- Component internals, nav chrome, icon spacing → Tailwind scale (`p-2`, `gap-8`).
- **Migration note:** old custom `p-24` meant 24px → use `p-6`; old `gap-64` meant 64px → use `gap-16`.

### 1.4 Horizontal page gutter

Always use `px-gutter` for horizontal page insets. This is a `clamp()` from
~20px to 80px that scales with viewport width.

```tsx
// ✅ correct — responsive inset
<main className="px-gutter max-w-page-lg mx-auto">

// ❌ wrong — fixed padding misses the clamp
<main className="px-4 max-w-page-lg mx-auto">
```

### 1.5 Max-width tokens

| Utility | Token | Value |
|---|---|---|
| `max-w-page-sm` | `--max-width-page-sm` | `800px` — long-form / case study |
| `max-w-page-md` | `--max-width-page-md` | `1000px` — standard content |
| `max-w-page-lg` | `--max-width-page-lg` | `1400px` — wide layout |
| `max-w-xl` | `--max-width-xl` | `1440px` — nav bar |

Never use `max-w-4xl`, `max-w-5xl`, etc. (Tailwind's rem-based scale).
Always use the project's named page widths above.

### 1.6 Border radius — Tailwind defaults only

Use Tailwind’s built-in `rounded-*` scale (no custom `@theme` radius tokens).

| Use case | Utility | Tailwind default (≈) |
|---|---|---|
| Small corners | `rounded-sm` | 2px |
| Medium corners (cards, hero box, buttons) | `rounded-lg` | 8px |
| Large / 24px corners | `rounded-3xl` | 24px |
| Pills / avatars | `rounded-full` | 50% |

Do not use custom `--radius-*` tokens or `rounded-md` for project medium radii — prefer `rounded-lg`.

### 1.7 Motion tokens

| Token | Value | Use for |
|---|---|---|
| `--transition-fast` | `150ms ease` | Hover states, opacity fades |

Use `transition-fast` as a CSS variable in the rare cases motion needs
to be expressed in CSS. For Tailwind, compose with `transition duration-[150ms] ease-in`.

### 1.8 Nav / layout system tokens

These are consumed by nav and layout components. Reference via CSS variable only
(they are not used as Tailwind utilities directly):

| Token | Value | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `--nav-z` | `55` | Nav sits between sky (`z-0`) and hero box (`z-60`) |
| `--nav-scroll-margin` | `4.75rem` | `scroll-margin-top` on anchor targets `#work`, `#visual` |
| `--nav-fill-background` | `color-mix` from `--color-fill-default` at 30% | Frosted glass nav fill |
| `--nav-fill-backdrop-blur` | `16px` | Backdrop blur for nav |
| `--nav-icon-size` | `32px` | Nav icon dimensions |
| `--gallery-row-height` | `45vh` | `GalleryRow` height |
| `--gallery-row-min-height` | `400px` | `GalleryRow` min-height |
| `--spacer-section-height` | `200px` | Vertical spacer sections |
| `--link-hover-opacity` | `0.7` | All link hover states |
| `--border-width-sm` | `0.5px` | All hairline borders/dividers |

**Never hardcode these values inline** — always reference the variable.

