## 2. TYPOGRAPHY — USE `@utility type-*` CLASSES

The project defines a complete type system via `@utility` in `src/styles/globals.css`.
These are the ONLY way to set typography. Never compose font size + weight +
line-height manually in className strings.

### 2.1 Type utility reference

| Utility | Use case | Font | Size | Weight |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `type-display` | Hero headline, page title | Serif | `--font-size-display` (48px→38px) | Light 300 |
| `type-page-heading` | Page-level `<h1>` | Serif | `--font-size-2xl` (28px) | Normal 400 |
| `type-h2` | Section headings | Serif | `--text-2xl` (24px) | Normal 400 |
| `type-proj-title` | Case study page `<h2>` | Sans | `--text-xl` (20px) | Medium 500 |
| `type-h3-subhead` | Sub-section headings | Sans | `--text-xl` (20px) | Medium 500 |
| `type-hero-description` | Hero `<h1>` descriptor | Sans | `--font-size-2xl` (28px) | Light 300 |
| `type-body` | Default body text | Sans | `--text-base` (16px) | Normal 400 |
| `type-body-bold` | Emphasized body | Sans | `--text-base` (16px) | Medium 500 |
| `type-body-sm` | Captions, labels, metadata | Sans | `--text-sm` (14px) | Normal 400 |
| `type-body-sm-bold` | Bold captions/labels | Sans | `--text-sm` (14px) | Medium 500 |
| `type-nav-link` | Navigation links | Sans | `--text-sm` (14px) | Medium 500 |

Use Tailwind `--font-weight-*` in utilities (`normal`, `medium`, `light`). For one-off
emphasis in JSX use `font-medium` (500), not `font-semibold` (600).

### 2.2 Type utility rules

```tsx
// ✅ correct
<h1 className="type-display text-text-default">Welcome</h1>
<p className="type-body text-text-subtle">Caption text</p>
<h2 className="type-h2 text-text-secondary">Section</h2>

// ❌ wrong — never manually compose typography
<h1 className="text-[48px] font-light leading-[1.05] tracking-[-3px] font-serif">
<p className="text-sm font-normal leading-[1.3]">
```

- A `type-*` utility sets `font`, `letter-spacing`, and `line-height` atomically.
  Do not override individual sub-properties (`leading-*`, `tracking-*`, `text-*`,
  `font-*`) on an element that already has a `type-*` class unless intentionally
  overriding for a one-off exception — document why.
- `type-display` is responsive: `font-size-display` reduces from 48px to 38px
  at ≤1280px automatically via the `:root` override. Do not add manual responsive
  size classes on top of it.
- Pair `type-*` with a color token: `type-body text-text-default`, `type-body-sm text-text-subtle`.

### 2.3 Fonts are loaded via `next/font`

```ts
// src/lib/fonts.ts — pattern
import localFont from "next/font/local";

export const saans = localFont({
  src: "...",
  variable: "--font-saans",
  display: "swap",
});
```

```tsx
// src/app/layout.tsx
import { saans, crimson } from "@/lib/fonts";

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en" className={`${saans.variable} ${crimson.variable}`}>
      <body>{children}</body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

