## 3. DIVIDERS & BORDERS

The project has a dedicated `@utility bottom-hr` for horizontal rules:

```tsx
// ✅ section divider
<hr className="bottom-hr" />

// ✅ border on a container — always use border-line token
<div className="border-b border-line">

// ❌ never
<div className="border-b border-gray-200">
<hr className="border-t border-[#d7d7d9]">
```

- All borders use `--border-width-sm` (0.5px) via `border-line`. Never write
  `border` without the `border-line` color token.
- For hairline borders on components use `border border-line`.

---

## 4. STYLING — TAILWIND UTILITIES + PROJECT TOKENS

### 4.1 CSS files

`src/styles/globals.css` is the **token + type system** file. Do not add new global CSS files.

- **Prefer Tailwind utilities in TSX** for layout, spacing, and color.
- **CSS modules** (`*.module.css`) are allowed only for effects that are awkward in utilities:
  keyframes, `animation-timeline`, masks, nav slide layers, cursor zones. Do not add new modules for simple layout.
- Avoid new `@apply` — extract a React component or use utilities instead.
- No `style={{ color: "..." }}` for values that have a project token.

Exceptions where `style={{}}` is permitted (comment why):
- Runtime-computed values: `style={{ width: `${pct}%` }}`
- CSS variables for assets: `style={{ "--hero-icon-url": "url(...)" } as CSSProperties}`
- Canvas/WebGL or third-party overrides

### 4.2 Class composition — always use `cn()`

```ts
// src/lib/utils.ts
import { clsx, type ClassValue } from "clsx";
import { twMerge } from "tailwind-merge";
export function cn(...inputs: ClassValue[]) {
  return twMerge(clsx(inputs));
}
```

```tsx
// ✅ correct
<div className={cn("type-body text-text-default px-gutter", isActive && "bg-fill-default")} />

// ❌ wrong
<div className={`type-body text-text-default px-gutter ${isActive ? "bg-fill-default" : ""}`} />
```

### 4.3 Link hover states

Use `--link-hover-opacity` (0.7) for all link hover effects:

```tsx
// ✅
<a className="transition-opacity hover:opacity-70">Link</a>

// ❌ — inventing a hover value
<a className="hover:opacity-50">Link</a>
```

---

## 5. WHEN TO EXTRACT A COMPONENT

Extract a component when ANY of these is true:

1. **Repetition** — the same className combination appears 2+ times across different files.
2. **Complexity** — more than ~8 utility classes on a single element AND it's a
   reusable pattern (not a one-off page layout).
3. **Behaviour** — the element has state, events, or accessibility requirements.

### Component hierarchy

| Layer | What lives here | Path |
|---|---|---|
| **Primitive** | Single-element, prop-driven (Button, Badge, Tag) | `src/components/ui/` |
| **Composite** | Combines primitives (Card, FormField, Modal) | `src/components/ui/` |
| **Feature** | Business-aware composites (ProjectCard, CaseStudyHero) | `src/components/[feature]/` |
| **Section** | Full-width layout blocks (HeroSection, Footer) | `src/components/sections/` |

### Do NOT componentise

- One-off layout containers with fewer than 5 classes.
- `<section className="px-gutter py-lg">` wrappers that appear once.
- Purely typographic `<p>` or `<span>` wrappers.

### Variants via `cva`, never duplicate files

```tsx
const button = cva(
  "inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg type-body-bold transition-opacity duration-[150ms] ease-in",
  {
    variants: {
      size: { sm: "h-8 px-3", md: "h-10 px-4", lg: "h-12 px-6" },
    },
  }
);
```

---

## 6. NEXT.JS APP ROUTER RULES

- Default to **Server Components**. `"use client"` only for hooks, browser APIs, or context.
- Keep `"use client"` as **leaf nodes** — not on `layout.tsx` or `page.tsx` unless required.
- Data fetching in Server Components (`async/await` in component).

```
src/styles/globals.css     ← tokens + @utility type-*

src/app/
  layout.tsx               ← font variables on <html>
  page.tsx

src/components/
  ui/ | sections/ | [feature]/

src/lib/
  utils.ts                 ← cn()
  fonts.ts
```

### Anchor scroll targets

`#work` and `#visual` have `scroll-margin-top: var(--nav-scroll-margin)` in `@layer base`.
Add new anchor ids there when sections sit under the fixed nav.

---

## 7. TYPESCRIPT RULES

- `interface` for props, `type` for unions. No `any`. No `enum` — use `as const`.
- Named exports in `components/`; default exports only for `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx`.

---

## 8. RESPONSIVENESS

- `px-gutter` and named spacers (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) are responsive via `:root` @media — don't duplicate with manual overrides.
- Layout breakpoints: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `max-sm:` per default Tailwind scale.
- `type-display` shrinks automatically — no `md:text-[38px]` on top.

---

## 9. ACCESSIBILITY

- Interactive elements: visible text or `aria-label`.
- Semantic HTML: `<button>`, `<a>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, etc.
- Do not remove global `:focus-visible` without a replacement.

---

